   "flags": {},
   "order": 6,
   "mode": 0,
   "properties": {},
   "title": "Read me",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Glitch only where the subject is\n\nSAM3 needs a finished picture, but the glitch happens *while* the picture is being made. So this graph works in two passes:\n\n1. **Pass 1 - clean** draws the picture normally.\n2. **SAM3** segments it (`bicycle`).\n3. **Pass 2 - glitched** re-denoises **only the masked region**, starting from pass 1's own latent.\n\n### Why it is not simply \"the same seed twice\"\n\nThe same seed does *not* give you the same picture back. Glitching the early steps changes the composition decisions themselves, and because every block is attention over all tokens, damage inside the mask spreads outside it on the very next block. A second full generation gives you a different bicycle.\n\n`Keep everything outside the mask` (`SetLatentNoiseMask`) is what fixes it: at every step the sampler keeps the new result inside the mask and restores pass 1's latent outside it. Outside the mask the picture is *identical*, not merely similar.\n\n### The denoise knob\n\nPass 2's `denoise` decides how much of the subject survives inside the mask:\n\n- `0.4-0.6` - the bicycle is clearly the same, damaged\n- `0.75` (default) - recognisably the same object, strongly distorted\n- `1.0` - the masked region is rebuilt from scratch; only the surroundings are preserved\n\nNote that `denoise` below 1 shortens the run, so the glitch node's `step_start`/`step_end` count steps actually sampled: at 8 steps and `denoise` 0.75 there are 6, and steps 0-2 are the first three of those.\n\n### It costs less than it looks\n\nComfyUI caches pass 1. Only the first queue pays for it - after that, changing strength, mode, `glitch_seed` or `denoise` re-runs the glitched pass alone.\n\n### Model\n\n`sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors` (1.75 GB) goes in `ComfyUI/models/checkpoints/`.\n\nhttps://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors\n\n### Prompt syntax (it is not a weight)\n\nMax **32 tokens**. Commas separate categories, and `:N` is **how many objects** to find, *not* a strength:\n\n```\nbicycle:2, window:4\n```\n\nParenthesised weights like `(bicycle:1.2)` are stripped.\n\n### Leave `individual_masks` off\n\nOn, it returns one mask **per object**, and the glitch node reads a stack of masks as *frames across the sampling steps* - so several objects would animate over the run instead of glitching several regions.\n\n### Notes\n\n- `Mask conditioning` grows the mask by 48 px (~3 tokens) and blurs it by 32 px (~2 tokens). The blur is what feathers the seam between glitched and untouched.\n- The mask is a **soft multiplier**, never thresholded: grey = partial glitch.\n- Empty mask? Lower `threshold` toward 0.3, or use a simpler noun.\n- Needs comfyui-kjnodes for `GrowMaskWithBlur` and `ImageAndMaskPreview`."
   ]
  },
